{
  "$comment": [
    "The Gearbox 1.3 ABI surface, frozen. NOT a copy of abi.json -- only the",
    "three things a COMPILED mod depends on: the import name, its wire",
    "signature, and the capability that gates it. Docs and parameter names may",
    "be reworded freely; those cannot break a .wasm that already exists.",
    "",
    "Derived from sdk/abi.json at tag gearbox-v1.3, the same way abi-1.2.json",
    "was derived from gearbox-v1.2. Written when 1.4 opened with monuments and",
    "the economy surface behind them -- sector taxes, the goods economy,",
    "directed factories, nationalisation -- and two battle reads. Everything",
    "listed here shipped in 1.3 and must keep working: within major version 1",
    "a symbol may be added but never renamed, re-signed, or re-gated.",
    "",
    "ONE ENTRY DIFFERS FROM THE TAG, on purpose. gearbox:country set_number was",
    "tagged as \"(iiid)i\", a typo: the WAMR signature alphabet is i/I/f/F and has",
    "no d, so the host entry never matched the import a compiled mod declares and",
    "the call trapped as unlinked (fixed in 25892ec, after the tag). What a 1.3",
    "binary actually imports is (i32, i32, i32, f64) -> i32, which is \"(iiiF)i\",",
    "and that is what this file freezes -- it records what a compiled mod depends",
    "on, and no compiled mod ever depended on the typo."
  ],
